# Storefront locale & checkout

## Header / locale
- Keep **language**, **deliver-to (country)**, and **currency** as **separate** controls.
- Changing **deliver-to** should set that country's default currency; changing currency alone must **not** change deliver-to.
- Selection changes should apply **immediately** (refresh/navigation as the app already does) without flash of wrong default when possible.
- Show country/currency clearly (name + code + flag where the UI already supports it).

## Checkout
- Do **not** ask for country again if deliver-to is already chosen in the header — drive address fields from deliver-to.
- Address fields are **country-specific** (e.g. US states dropdown).
- Phone: separate country-code control + **numeric-only** national number; keep dial dropdown compact.
- Preserve user-entered checkout fields across deliver-to refresh when the app supports draft persistence.
- Customer account area and admin must stay **isolated** (roles/routes must not mix).

## Data
- Prices/formatting follow selected currency; copy follows selected language via next-intl.
